WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.340
[intro music]

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.900
Good morning, Hank, it's
Wednesday, February 7th,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.180
and it's story day.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.280
Our story today is called,

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.400
"Everyone Poops in my Pants"

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.680
by Hank Green.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.820
My name is Hank,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.580
and I have a small problem:

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.760
everyone poops in my pants.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.300
Each morning, I wake up

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.560
and dozens of people surround my house,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.340
chanting,

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.960
"What do we want to poop in?"

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.380
"Hank's pants!"

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.360
"When do we want to poop in them?"

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.500
"Now!"

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.320
[chants] "Hey hey! Ho ho!

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.980
Into Hank's pants we gotta go!

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.700
Hey hey! Ho ho!

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.680
Into Hank's pants we gotta go...

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:43.380
poop."

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.260
Now, I know what you are thinking.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.260
You are thinking,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.620
Hank, I believe that many people

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.380
have pooped in your pants.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.020
But I remain unconvinced that everyone

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.720
has pooped in your pants.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.840
And that is true enough.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.680
For instance, many poor people
haven't pooped in my pants

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.320
because they lack the resources
to fly to Montana.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.540
And many babies haven't
pooped in my pants

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.720
because they're too busy
pooping in their own.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.720
I'm just saying that, statistically,

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.800
an improbably large number of
people have pooped in my pants.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.200
My mom and dad, and my brother, John,

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.080
have all pooped in my pants.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.700
Kirsten Dunst

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.720
was wearing, and pooping in,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.900
my pants during the entire
filming of Spider Man 2.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.160
The entire Liverpool Football Club

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.140
pooped in my umbros immediately after
winning the 2005 UEFA Cup.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.420
German novelist Günter Grass

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.520
pooped in my pants while
wearing his Nobel Prize.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.980
Stephen Dedalus

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.940
is just one of the many fictional characters
who have non-fictionally pooped

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.280
in my non-fictional pants.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.180
Al Roker

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.080
had my pants tailored to fit him

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.820
and then pooped in them.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.580
Vladimir Ilyich Lenin

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.340
died in 1924

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.180
but has, nonetheless, pooped in my pants.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.800
George W. Bush

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.720
is so incompetent

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.140
that he failed to poop

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.240
IN my pants,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.460
although he did poop

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.120
NEAR my pants

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.900
and then later claimed

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.320
that he had never intended
to poop in my pants

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.460
and that no one in his administration

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.360
had EVER talked about pooping

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.540
IN ANYONE'S pants.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.020
Having seen his poop,

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.140
I can report that it looks exactly

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:19.780
like bullshit.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.540
Wow, those guys must be selling
the President's war plan.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.600
People often ask me, "Hank,

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.520
does it bother you that everyone
poops in your pants?"

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.040
Yes, it does.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.900
Sometimes something great will happen,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.460
like, the other day Barack Obama came by, and

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.900
he pooped in my pants,

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.880
and his poop kind of makes me
believe in America again.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:39.980
But, mostly,

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.420
I dislike having people poop in my pants.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.440
But everyone has a cross to bear.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.520
Some people have chronic back pain,

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.600
some people are on Team Karen,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.600
some people are Republicans.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.340
Me,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:55.660
I just happen to have pants into
which people really like to poop.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.780
It could certainly be worse.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.300
It's like Monty Python member
Eric Idle once told me,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.000
while he was pooping in my pants,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.760
[music] Eric Idle [singing] - "Always look on the
bright side of life."

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.540
[music continues, accompanied by whistling]

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.540
Hank, per the request of several commenters,

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.860
I hereby challenge you

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.840
to answer every single question in your survey

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.040
in one video blog

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.780
of 3 minutes and 30 seconds or less.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.700
Yes, you will have to talk at this speed.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.400
Hank, I'll see you tomorrow.

